    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nPositioned on an exceptional, private and landscaped site, this outstanding five bedroom detached family home is a must view to truly appreciate its fantastic location on the Lower Road, Bunratty, Co Clare. Arriving at the property the wraparound sweeping tarmacadam drive bound by mature trees and manicured lawns leads to the extended front and side drive. The interior of the home offers bright, spacious, well proportioned and extensive living accommodation with the ground floor boasting main entrance porchway, entrance hallway, kitchen/breakfast, formal dining with open plan to family room, two additional receptions, ground floor WC, sauna and jacuzzi room and bedroom one/home office which compliment four further double bedrooms at first floor level and home office positioned to the first floor also. Extensive timber flooring, quality carpets, tiling and built in wardrobes feature throughout, solid shaker maple kitchen, two solid fuel stoves, one which has integrated back boiler and so much more to be appreciated at time of view. To the exterior, dry stone walls, hard surface tennis court, extensive patio and split level lawns, vegetable plot, storage sheds and adjoining garage concludes what can only be described as the perfect family home just three minutes by car to the renowned Bunratty, ease of access to the N18 for those commuting to Shannon, Limerick, Ennis and Galway with viewing highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL 002295"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 3.12m x 1m\nQuality tiled flooring, wall mounted lighting, feature window to front gardens with glass panel teak door leading to main entrance hallway and Georgian glass panel door leading to office.\n\nEntrance Hallway - 3.12m x 2.6m\nQuality tiled flooring, split level polished rail stairs leading to first floor landing with feature void between ground and first floor and glass panel door leading to main reception and door to kitchen.\n\nReception Room - 5.5m x 3.7m\nSolid oak polished timber flooring, marble surround feature fireplace with marble insert and polished marble flag, decorative ceiling coving with centre rose feature and connecting Georgian glass panel door to formal dining.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast - 4.9m x 3.7m\nModern shaker maple built in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, one and a half bowl single drainer sink with mixer tap, integrated five ring gas hob with extractor hood and fan, double fan assisted ovens with overhead indentation for microwave, space for double fridge freezer, tiled splashback surround, quality tiled flooring, wall mounted shelving, tv point and connecting doors to utility and formal dining.\n\nDining Room (open plan into Family Room) - 7.5m x 3.45m\nDining area - quality tiled flooring, decorative ceiling coving with centre rose feature and open arch to family room. Family Room - quality tiled flooring, wrap around feature windows to landscaped gardens with French doors onto extensive paved patio and freestanding solid fuel Stanley stove with marble surround.\n\nUtility Room - 3.6m x 2.8m\nBuilt in wall and base units with ample work surfaces, one and a half bowl single drainer sink with mixer tap, space and plumbing for washing machine and dryer, quality tiled flooring, doors to built in cloakroom with additional overhead and base storage with further side exposed shelving and connecting doors to bedroom one/home office, ground floor WC and reception two.\n\nBedroom One/Home Office - 5m x 3.25m\nOak style timber flooring, ample built in ceiling to floor shelving with integrated study desk and feature window to front gardens.\n\nReception Two - 6.3m x 3.2m\nWall to wall and ceiling to floor built in units with eye level glass display, additional overhead and base storage, decorative ceiling coving, wall mounted lighting, integrated solid fuel stove (with back boiler), connecting door to wellness room\n\nWellness Room - 3.65m x 2.9m\nQuality ceiling to floor tiling, double integrated jacuzzi bath, door to three person sauna and connecting door to adjoining garage.\n\nAdjoining Garage - 4m x 4m\nDouble connecting doors to front drive, stira stairs leading to additional attic storage, ample wall mounted shelving and electrical socket points.\n\nGround Floor WC - 2.4m x 1.28m\nLow level WC, wash hand basin with overhead wall mounted mirrored storage cabinet and quality wall and floor tiling.\n\nFirst Floor Landing - 5.1m x 3.43m\nQuality carpeted flooring, decorative ceiling coving with centre rose feature, triple doors to hotpress housing immersion tank and shelving and doors leading to bedrooms two, three, four and five, home office and main bathroom.\n\nBedroom Two - 4m x 3.66m\nQuality carpeted flooring, ample built in wardrobes with integrated shelving and overhead and base storage and connecting door to ensuite.\n\nEnsuite - 2m x 1.5m\nLow level WC, wash hand basin with overhead wall mounted mirror unit and double press base storage, shower tray with overhead pumped shower and wall and floor tiling.\n\nBedroom Three - 3.65m x 3.5m\nQuality carpeted flooring, built in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and additional overhead and base storage and integrated shelving with side vanity with base exposed shelving, overhead wall mounted mirror and wall lighting.\n\nBathroom - 2.8m x 2.1m\nLow level WC, integrated wash hand basin with built in storage base with side drawers, overhead wall mounted mirror unit and electric shaver point and light, bidet with mixer tap and panel bath with overhead shower attachment with glass panel shower door and quality wall and floor tiling.\n\nHome Office - 2.72m x 2.31m\nWall to wall and ceiling to floor built in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and additional overhead and base storage and integrated shelving.\n\nBedroom Four - 3.6m x 2.72m\nQuality carpeted flooring.\n\nBedroom Five - 3.6m x 3.1m\nQuality carpeted flooring and built in wardrobes with ample hanging rails and additional overhead and base storage.\n\n"
      },
